('piles','Piles (Hemorrhoids)','Clinically assessed, Kshara Sutra-informed care for piles and related conditions.','ShieldPlus','Ano-rectal Disorders',true,'/piles-treatment',false,true,1,'Piles (Hemorrhoids) affects the anorectal region and is often linked to digestion, bowel habits, and prolonged strain. Ayurveda''s Kshara Sutra and allied approaches are well known for anorectal conditions, alongside dietary and lifestyle correction.','["Pain or discomfort during or after bowel movements","Bleeding during bowel movements","A feeling of incomplete evacuation","Swelling, itching, or irritation near the anus","Straining or difficulty passing stool"]'::jsonb,'["Chronic constipation or straining","Low-fibre diet and inadequate hydration","Prolonged sitting or sedentary habits","Pregnancy or increased abdominal pressure","Ignoring the natural urge to pass stool"]'::jsonb,'Care may include internal herbal formulations, dietary correction to ease bowel movements, and, where appropriate, procedures such as Kshara Sutra therapy, decided after a detailed clinical examination.','["Avoid straining and respond promptly to the urge to pass stool","Avoid prolonged sitting, especially on hard surfaces","Stay physically active with regular gentle movement","Maintain good hygiene in the affected area","Avoid self-medicating without a clinical examination"]'::jsonb,'["Increase fibre intake through vegetables, fruits, and whole grains","Drink adequate water through the day","Limit spicy and heavily fried foods","Avoid excess tea, coffee, or alcohol if they worsen symptoms","Include soaked dry fruits or flaxseed as a natural stool softener where suitable"]'::jsonb,'[{"q":"Can Ayurveda help manage piles (hemorrhoids)?","a":"Yes. Ayurvedic care for piles (hemorrhoids) focuses on personalised herbal formulations and lifestyle correction aimed at long-term management and symptom relief. Dr. Pratibha Y.C. will assess your specific case in consultation before recommending a plan."},{"q":"How long does treatment usually take to show results?","a":"This varies by individual and severity. Many patients notice initial improvement within a few weeks, with a fuller management plan typically reviewed over 2–3 months. Your exact timeline will be discussed at consultation."},{"q":"Is this treatment suitable alongside my current medication?","a":"Ayurvedic care can often be planned alongside conventional treatment. Please share your current medications and reports during consultation so the plan can be coordinated safely."},{"q":"Do I need to visit the clinic in person?","a":"Both clinic and online consultations are available. Certain examinations or therapies may require an in-person visit, which will be advised if relevant to your case."}]'::jsonb,now()),
