('rheumatoid-arthritis','Rheumatoid Arthritis','Supportive, coordinated care to ease stiffness and joint inflammation.','Bone','Joint Disorders',false,null,false,true,8,'Rheumatoid Arthritis involves stiffness, swelling, or pain in the joints that can affect mobility and daily activity. Ayurveda views most joint conditions through the lens of Vata imbalance and Ama (metabolic toxin) accumulation, and addresses both the discomfort and the underlying contributing factors.','["Joint stiffness, especially in the morning","Swelling or tenderness around affected joints","Pain that worsens with cold weather or exertion","Reduced range of motion","Occasional warmth or mild inflammation at the joint"]'::jsonb,'["Age-related wear on joint tissue","Sedentary lifestyle or prolonged joint strain","Poor metabolism leading to Ama accumulation","Nutrient deficiencies affecting joint health","Aggravated Vata dosha from irregular routine"]'::jsonb,'Care typically includes internal herbal formulations to reduce stiffness and support joint nourishment, external therapies where suitable, and guidance on movement and posture. Panchakarma-based approaches may be recommended for appropriate cases after assessment.','["Keep joints warm, particularly in cold or damp weather","Include gentle daily movement such as walking or stretching","Avoid prolonged sitting or standing in one position","Maintain a healthy body weight to reduce joint load","Use supportive footwear and correct posture"]'::jsonb,'["Favour warm, unctuous, well-cooked meals","Include anti-inflammatory spices like turmeric and ginger","Reduce cold, raw, and excessively dry foods","Stay adequately hydrated with warm fluids","Limit processed and refined foods"]'::jsonb,'[{"q":"Can Ayurveda help manage rheumatoid arthritis?","a":"Yes. Ayurvedic care for rheumatoid arthritis focuses on personalised herbal formulations and lifestyle correction aimed at long-term management and symptom relief. Dr. Pratibha Y.C. will assess your specific case in consultation before recommending a plan."},{"q":"How long does treatment usually take to show results?","a":"This varies by individual and severity. Many patients notice initial improvement within a few weeks, with a fuller management plan typically reviewed over 2–3 months. Your exact timeline will be discussed at consultation."},{"q":"Is this treatment suitable alongside my current medication?","a":"Ayurvedic care can often be planned alongside conventional treatment. Please share your current medications and reports during consultation so the plan can be coordinated safely."},{"q":"Do I need to visit the clinic in person?","a":"Both clinic and online consultations are available. Certain examinations or therapies may require an in-person visit, which will be advised if relevant to your case."}]'::jsonb,now()),
