Rather than only calming the skin from the outside, an Ayurvedic plan typically starts with an assessment of your digestive strength and the factors triggering flare-ups, whether that''s diet, stress, season change, or a combination.

Internal formulations are chosen to support detoxification and reduce the inflammatory pattern associated with psoriasis, while external applications help soothe active patches. Diet correction, particularly avoiding incompatible food combinations and excess processed food, plays a meaningful supporting role.

Consistency matters more than intensity here. A realistic, personalised plan that you can sustain through season changes tends to outperform an aggressive short course that''s hard to maintain.','Skin Health','Dr. Pratibha Y.C.',true,0,'[{"q":"Can psoriasis be fully cured with Ayurveda?","a":"Ayurveda focuses on long-term management and reducing flare-ups rather than promising a permanent cure. Many patients see significant improvement in symptom severity and frequency with consistent care."},{"q":"How long before I see improvement?","a":"Most patients begin noticing changes in skin comfort within 4–6 weeks, with fuller results typically assessed over 3 months."}]'::jsonb,'Ayurvedic Treatment for Psoriasis | Dr. Pratibha Y.C.','Understand how Ayurveda approaches psoriasis, from internal detoxification to diet and daily routine, explained by Dr. Pratibha Y.C., BAMS, MD (Kayachikitsa).','2026-05-12'::timestamptz),
('Ayurvedic Treatment for Piles: Kshara Sutra and Beyond','ayurvedic-treatment-for-piles','From dietary correction to Kshara Sutra therapy, here''s what an Ayurvedic approach to piles actually involves.','Piles, or hemorrhoids, are closely linked to bowel habits, diet, and prolonged strain. Before reaching for any procedure, Ayurvedic care typically starts with correcting the factors that caused the swelling and irritation in the first place, chiefly constipation and low-fibre diets.

Kshara Sutra is one of Ayurveda''s most well-documented contributions to anorectal care, a thread medicated with herbal preparations used to treat fistula and select piles cases. It''s a specific clinical procedure recommended only after a proper in-person examination.

For many patients, especially in early stages, a combination of fibre-rich diet, adequate hydration, internal herbal formulations, and bowel-habit correction is enough to bring lasting relief.

Whatever the stage, an honest clinical assessment is the right starting point, since piles, fissures, and fistula can present similarly but need different care.','Anorectal Care','Dr. Pratibha Y.C.',true,1,'[{"q":"Is Kshara Sutra therapy painful?","a":"The procedure is performed with appropriate local care and is generally well tolerated. Your physician will explain the process and aftercare in detail before proceeding."},{"q":"Can piles be managed without surgery?","a":"Many cases, particularly in earlier stages, respond well to dietary correction and internal Ayurvedic care. More advanced cases may benefit from procedures like Kshara Sutra, decided after clinical examination."}]'::jsonb,'Ayurvedic Treatment for Piles (Hemorrhoids) | Dr. Pratibha Y.C.','A clear look at how Ayurveda, including Kshara Sutra therapy, approaches piles and related anorectal conditions.','2026-04-28'::timestamptz),
('Natural Ways to Improve Digestion, According to Ayurveda','natural-ways-to-improve-digestion','Strong digestion (Agni) is the foundation Ayurveda builds every other treatment on. Here''s where to start.','In Ayurveda, digestion isn''t just about avoiding an upset stomach, it''s considered the foundation that everything else, energy, immunity, skin, mood, is built on.

A few habits go a long way: eating at consistent times, avoiding cold drinks with meals, and giving your last meal enough time to digest before sleep. None of these are dramatic changes, but consistency compounds.

Warm water sipped through the day, a short walk after meals, and everyday spices like ginger, cumin, and fennel all support digestive fire in small, sustainable ways.

Where digestion has been struggling for a while, bloating, irregularity, acidity, a personalised consultation can identify what''s specifically off balance and build a targeted plan around it.','Digestive Health','Dr. Pratibha Y.C.',true,2,'[{"q":"What is Agni in Ayurveda?","a":"Agni refers to digestive fire, the body''s capacity to process and absorb food. Strong, balanced Agni is considered central to overall health in Ayurveda."},{"q":"Are digestive herbs safe for daily use?","a":"Many culinary spices used for digestion, like cumin and fennel, are safe for regular use. Specific herbal formulations should be taken under guidance based on your constitution and condition."}]'::jsonb,'Natural Ways to Improve Digestion | Ayurvedic Guidance','Simple, sustainable Ayurvedic habits to strengthen digestion and reduce bloating, acidity, and irregularity.','2026-04-10'::timestamptz),
('Managing Arthritis with Ayurveda: A Practical Guide','managing-arthritis-with-ayurveda','Joint stiffness and pain respond well to a combination of internal care, diet, and consistent movement.','Arthritis in Ayurveda is largely understood through Vata imbalance and the accumulation of Ama, a byproduct of poor digestion that tends to settle in joints and cause stiffness.

Warmth matters here, keeping joints protected from cold and damp conditions, using warm oil application where suitable, and favouring warm, well-cooked meals over cold or raw foods.

Gentle, regular movement keeps joints from stiffening further, while targeted herbal formulations aim to reduce inflammation and support joint tissue over time.

As with most chronic conditions, the plan is adjusted as your joints respond, and coordinated with any existing medical treatment you''re already on.','Joint Health','Dr. Pratibha Y.C.',true,3,'[{"q":"Does Ayurveda help with rheumatoid arthritis specifically?","a":"Ayurvedic care can offer supportive management for symptoms and inflammation alongside your rheumatologist''s treatment. It should complement, not replace, prescribed medical care."},{"q":"Is exercise recommended during joint pain flare-ups?","a":"Gentle, appropriate movement is generally encouraged, but intensity should be adjusted during active flare-ups. Your physician can guide what''s suitable for your stage."}]'::jsonb,'Managing Arthritis with Ayurveda | Dr. Pratibha Y.C.','How Ayurveda approaches arthritis and joint pain through herbal support, diet, and daily movement.','2026-03-22'::timestamptz),
('Ayurvedic Diet for Diabetes Management','ayurvedic-diet-for-diabetes','Diet plays a central supporting role in diabetes management. Here''s how Ayurveda frames food choices.','Diabetes management in Ayurveda is approached as a long-term metabolic balancing act, not a quick fix, and diet is one of its most practical levers.

Whole grains, legumes, and fibre-rich vegetables are favoured over refined carbohydrates, both for their slower glucose release and their support of healthy digestion.

Meal timing matters as much as meal content. Regular, evenly spaced meals help avoid the swings that come from skipping meals and overeating later.

This dietary guidance works best alongside your prescribed medication and regular monitoring, never as a substitute for either.','Metabolic Health','Dr. Pratibha Y.C.',true,4,'[{"q":"Can Ayurvedic diet replace my diabetes medication?","a":"No. Dietary guidance is meant to support, not replace, prescribed medication and monitoring. Please continue your physician''s treatment plan alongside any dietary changes."},{"q":"Are there specific foods Ayurveda recommends avoiding?","a":"Refined sugar, white flour, and heavily processed foods are generally discouraged, along with irregular meal timing that causes blood sugar spikes."}]'::jsonb,'Ayurvedic Diet for Diabetes | Dr. Pratibha Y.C.','Practical, Ayurveda-informed dietary guidance to support blood sugar management alongside your medical care.','2026-03-05'::timestamptz),
('PCOS Management Naturally: An Ayurvedic Perspective','pcos-management-naturally','PCOS responds well to a combined approach: routine, diet, movement, and personalised herbal care.','PCOD/PCOS sits at the intersection of hormones, metabolism, and daily routine, which is exactly where Ayurveda''s whole-person approach tends to be useful.

A consistent daily schedule, sleep, meals, and activity, at similar times each day helps regulate the hormonal signalling that PCOS often disrupts.

Dietary correction focuses on stabilising blood sugar and supporting healthy digestion, since insulin resistance is closely linked to PCOS in many cases.

Personalised herbal formulations are chosen based on your specific symptom pattern, whether that''s irregular cycles, acne, weight changes, or a combination, and reviewed as your cycle responds.','Women''s Wellness','Dr. Pratibha Y.C.',true,5,'[{"q":"Can PCOS symptoms improve without hormonal medication?","a":"Many patients see improvement in cycle regularity and symptoms through lifestyle and Ayurvedic care, though some cases still need coordinated medical management. A personalised assessment will clarify what''s right for you."},{"q":"How does stress affect PCOS?","a":"Chronic stress can worsen hormonal imbalance, which is why stress management is typically built into a PCOS care plan alongside diet and herbal support."}]'::jsonb,'PCOS Management Naturally | Ayurvedic Women''s Health','How Ayurveda approaches PCOD/PCOS through cycle-aware lifestyle guidance and personalised herbal support.','2026-02-18'::timestamptz),
('Seasonal Immunity Tips from Ayurveda','seasonal-immunity-tips','Ayurveda treats immunity as something that shifts with the seasons. Here''s how to stay ahead of it.','Ayurveda has always treated immunity as seasonal rather than fixed, adjusting diet and routine (Ritucharya) as the weather shifts.

Warm, freshly cooked food, adequate rest, and gentle daily movement form the baseline across most seasons, with specific spices and herbs added depending on whether the season calls for warming or cooling support.

Sudden temperature changes, monsoon dampness, or peak summer heat each call for slightly different precautions, from hydration habits to what''s on your plate.

For anyone with recurring seasonal illness, colds, allergies, fatigue, a personalised Rasayana plan can help build resilience ahead of the season rather than reacting once symptoms appear.','Immunity','Dr. Pratibha Y.C.',true,6,'[{"q":"What is Rasayana therapy?","a":"Rasayana refers to Ayurvedic rejuvenation therapies aimed at building strength, immunity, and vitality, often using specific herbal formulations suited to the season and individual."},{"q":"Should immunity routines change with season?","a":"Yes, Ayurveda recommends adjusting diet and daily routine (Ritucharya) with each season to stay aligned with the body''s changing needs."}]'::jsonb,'Seasonal Immunity Tips | Ayurvedic Guidance','Simple, season-specific Ayurvedic habits to keep immunity strong through the year.','2026-01-30'::timestamptz),
('The Benefits of Panchakarma, Explained Simply','benefits-of-panchakarma','Panchakarma is often misunderstood as a generic detox. Here''s what it actually involves.','Panchakarma refers to five specific detoxification therapies in classical Ayurveda, not a single generic ''cleanse.'' Each therapy targets a particular pathway in the body and is chosen based on individual need.

Before any Panchakarma protocol begins, a preparatory phase (Purvakarma) using internal oleation and gentle heat therapy readies the body for the main procedures.

The therapies themselves are selected based on your constitution, current imbalance, and health goals, whether that''s supporting joint health, digestion, skin, or general rejuvenation.

Because Panchakarma involves real physiological effects, it''s recommended only after a proper consultation and is best undertaken under direct clinical supervision.','Panchakarma','Dr. Pratibha Y.C.',true,7,'[{"q":"Is Panchakarma suitable for everyone?","a":"Not automatically. Suitability depends on your constitution, current health status, and specific condition, which is assessed during consultation before recommending any Panchakarma protocol."},{"q":"How long does a Panchakarma program take?","a":"Duration varies widely based on the therapies involved and your individual plan, ranging from a few days to a few weeks."}]'::jsonb,'Benefits of Panchakarma | Ayurvedic Detox Therapy','What Panchakarma actually involves and who it''s typically recommended for.','2026-01-14'::timestamptz),
('Stress Management Through Ayurveda','stress-management-through-ayurveda','Chronic stress shows up in sleep, digestion, and mood alike. Ayurveda addresses it from several angles at once.','Chronic stress rarely stays contained to the mind, it shows up in sleep quality, digestion, and even skin health, which is why Ayurveda treats it as a whole-body concern.

A steady daily routine (Dinacharya), consistent wake and sleep times, regular meals, is one of the simplest and most effective stabilisers available.

Calming herbal formulations, along with practices like Pranayama (breathing exercises) and short mindfulness sessions, are typically layered onto this routine for added support.

Where stress has become significant or persistent, coordinating Ayurvedic support with a mental health professional gives the most complete care.','Mind & Wellness','Dr. Pratibha Y.C.',true,8,'[{"q":"Can Ayurveda help with anxiety alongside therapy?","a":"Yes, Ayurvedic lifestyle and herbal support can complement professional mental health care. It isn''t a substitute for therapy or psychiatric treatment where that''s needed."},{"q":"What daily practice helps most with stress?","a":"A consistent sleep schedule combined with a short daily breathing or mindfulness practice tends to make a noticeable difference for most patients."}]'::jsonb,'Stress Management Through Ayurveda | Dr. Pratibha Y.C.','Practical Ayurvedic approaches to managing chronic stress, from daily routine to herbal support.','2025-12-20'::timestamptz),
('Healthy Lifestyle According to Ayurveda: The Daily Basics','healthy-lifestyle-according-to-ayurveda','Most Ayurvedic treatment plans rest on the same foundation: a well-structured daily routine. Here''s what that looks like.','Underneath most Ayurvedic treatment plans is the same foundation: a daily routine (Dinacharya) that keeps the body''s natural rhythms steady.

Waking and sleeping at consistent times, eating meals at regular intervals, and getting some form of daily movement are the basics that everything else builds on.

Small additions, warm water in the morning, a few minutes of mindful breathing, avoiding screens right before bed, tend to compound meaningfully over weeks and months.

This foundation matters whether you''re managing a specific condition or simply aiming to stay well, and it''s usually the first thing addressed in any personalised consultation.','Lifestyle','Dr. Pratibha Y.C.',true,9,'[{"q":"What is Dinacharya?","a":"Dinacharya is the Ayurvedic concept of an ideal daily routine, covering wake time, meals, activity, and sleep, designed to keep the body''s rhythms in balance."},{"q":"Do I need to follow every recommendation to see benefit?","a":"No. Starting with one or two consistent changes, like a fixed sleep time or regular meal schedule, often brings noticeable benefit before adding more."}]'::jsonb,'Healthy Lifestyle According to Ayurveda | Daily Routine Guide','The foundational daily habits (Dinacharya) Ayurveda recommends for long-term health.','2025-12-02'::timestamptz)
